##Sept 29  
I've been intruiged about a tool since a few days. It's called HeyClickey. It's a macOS only tool but what it basically does is that it enables you to instantly snip any part of your screen and  
instantaneously ask any query related to it, I think using voice command. I found it very interesting because it had lots and lots of practical use in my life as well. So...I made it. Or should I say perhaps,  
a close working model of it. I learnt about how it worked and learnt about what techstack it needed and got to work and within a span of 3 days in which I only worked on this for 2 days, I have it working today.  
I press 3 keys like a keybind and I can screen clip a part of my screen and the AI locally tells me whatever I wanna know about it. I can also use it if I don't have any screen clipping to give it.  It's basically  
just AI but on your PC locally, even though it's a bit more complicated than that. I made the user enter an API key through which the app connects the Google Gemini Model to your app and then you can ask the  
queries. Pretty cool right? It's quick and you don't even need to open safari, then google gemini, the put your screenshot, then ask. It's a quick 3 step process. Once you give your API key to it, you're ready to  
go. I learnt a lot through this. I wrote the code myself by learning, googling and with the help of AI by asking what should I do if I wanna add this feature. It took a lot of frustration, errors, learning  
but eventually I did reach at a point where my product is working even though it only works locally on my own PC right now. I was looking for a project to make and see how inspiration can strike from the  
smallest of things. I'm happy to have reached this point where I learnt more about stuff and actually used it in practical use in a project where I can use it regularly and make it better in the process  
